ence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "California remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states at the presidential level, with a partisan lean of roughly twelve points toward Democrats. The incumbent president is term-limited, so neither party enters with an incumbency advantage. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market pricing are available for this race yet, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan fundamentals.\n\nRecent coverage centers on the 2028 primaries, with Governor Newsom, former Vice President Harris, and Vice President Vance dominating the discussion, but primary positioning says little about how California will vote in the general election. The state's reliable Democratic margin means a Republican win would require a substantial national shift. Expect a solid Democratic margin here, with uncertainty remaining wide until actual general-election polling appears.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9157, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8615, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8622, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8693, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8671, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8635, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8619, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8672, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8647, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.864, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8607, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.858, "margin": 12.0}]}